root
  html tag="script" lang="ts"
  line_break
  line_break
  html tag="ArticleMain" pane_path="docs / faq" title="frequently asked" subtitle="Short answers to the things that come up most often. If something here is wrong or missing, the source for this page lives in <code>docs/faq.md</code>."
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "shiki()"
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Twinkleplop is significantly "
          strong_emphasis
            strong_emphasis
              text "smaller"
          text " than Shiki and an order of magnitude faster. It offers similar quality highlighting in terms of correctness and granularity and also offers a similar toolkit for authoring code snippets."
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Unlike Shiki, Twinkleplop owns "
          emphasis
            text "most"
          text " of its stack, grammars are bespoke and not a downstream concern. Bugs in twinkleplop are bugs in twinkleplop."
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "prism()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Twinkleplop is a little larger than Prism but faster (the delta is not as great as against shiki, 3-6x typically). Twinkleplop is ESM and bundler friendly, and treeshakable."
          soft_break
          text "		Twinkleplop typically provides higher quality highlighting than Prism and a much richer toolkit. Twinkleplop also supports all features in all environments."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_install()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Pick a package manager. Both the core and any language modules are published under the"
          soft_break
          text "			"
          html tag="code"
            text "@twinkleplop"
          text " scope."
        line_break
        line_break
        html tag="CodeBlock" fname="install.sh" lang="shell" html=[object Object] self_closing=true
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "That's it — no peer dependencies, no postinstall scripts, no native bindings."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_runtimes()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Both. Every package ships ESM, CJS, and a browser-ready IIFE. There are no Node-only APIs in"
          soft_break
          text "			the runtime path, so the same import works in a Worker, a Cloudflare edge function, or a"
          soft_break
          text "			vanilla "
          html tag="code"
            text "&lt;script&gt;"
          text " tag."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_one_per_lang()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Languages are self-contained packages. You install and import only what you need, and"
          soft_break
          text "			tree-shaking does the rest. A page that highlights only HTML doesn't pay for the TypeScript"
          soft_break
          text "			grammar."
        line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Embedded languages — say, JS inside an HTML "
          html tag="code"
            text "&lt;script&gt;"
          text " tag — are an"
          soft_break
          text "			implementation detail of the parent language. You don't import them separately."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_lazy()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Yes. Every language package is a default-exported factory, so dynamic "
          html tag="code"
            text "import()"
          soft_break
          text "			works out of the box:"
        line_break
        line_break
        html tag="CodeBlock" fname="lazy.ts" lang="typescript" html=[object Object] self_closing=true
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Use this when the language depends on user input — an in-browser playground, for example —"
          soft_break
          text "			and you'd rather not ship every grammar up front."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_supported()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "The first-party set covers most of what you'd want for a docs site or a code-review UI:"
        line_break
        html tag="ul"
          line_break
          html tag="li"
            paragraph
              text "html, css, javascript, typescript, jsx, tsx"
          line_break
          html tag="li"
            paragraph
              text "json, yaml, toml, markdown, mdx"
          line_break
          html tag="li"
            paragraph
              text "rust, go, python, ruby, swift"
          line_break
          html tag="li"
            paragraph
              text "shell, sql, graphql, dockerfile"
          line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Anything else lives in "
          html tag="code"
            text "@twinkleplop-community/"
            text "*"
          text ". Grammars there follow the same"
          soft_break
          text "			shape and are loaded the same way."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_html_or_tokens()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Both. The default export gives you a highlighter that returns HTML; the"
          soft_break
          text "			"
          html tag="code"
            text "tokenizer"
          text " export gives you the raw token stream for custom rendering."
        line_break
        line_break
        html tag="CodeBlock" fname="tokenize.ts" lang="typescript" html=[object Object] self_closing=true
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Tokens are a flat array of "
          html tag="code"
            text "&#123; type, value, range &#125;"
          text " — no DOM, no React,"
          soft_break
          text "			no opinions. Render them however you like."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_themes()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Themes are CSS. The highlighter emits stable class names per token type"
          soft_break
          text "			("
          html tag="code"
            text ".tok-kw"
          text ", "
          html tag="code"
            text ".tok-str"
          text ", etc.) and ships a handful of starter sheets"
          soft_break
          text "			you can import or override."
        line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "If you want to swap themes at runtime, toggle a class on a parent element and let the"
          soft_break
          text "			cascade do the work — there's no JS theme registry to fight with."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_buildtime()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "That's the recommended path for static sites. The same packages run in Node, Bun, or Deno,"
          soft_break
          text "			so you can pre-render every code block at build time and ship zero runtime JS."
        line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "There are integrations for Astro, Eleventy, Next.js, and Vite under"
          soft_break
          text "			"
          html tag="code"
            text "@twinkleplop/integrations/"
            text "*"
          text "."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_size()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Core is roughly 4kb min+gzip. Each language adds between 2–9kb depending on grammar"
          soft_break
          text "			complexity. There is no shared regex blob — grammars are pre-compiled to small state"
          soft_break
          text "			machines at build time."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_keystroke()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "For most editor-sized inputs, yes. Tokenization is incremental: re-running the tokenizer on"
          soft_break
          text "			a slightly changed string reuses the previous run's state where it can."
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "If you're highlighting a 50,000-line file on every keystroke, you'll want to debounce"
          soft_break
          text "			regardless of which library you pick."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_add_lang()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Fork the monorepo, copy "
          html tag="code"
            text "packages/"
            text "_template"
          text ", and write a grammar in the small"
          soft_break
          text "			DSL described in the contributor guide. Snapshot tests run against a fixtures directory of"
          soft_break
          text "			real-world code."
        line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "If you want to publish under "
          html tag="code"
            text "@twinkleplop-community/"
            text "*"
          text ", open an issue first so"
          soft_break
          text "			we can reserve the package name."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    svelte_block tag="snippet"
      svelte_branch tag="snippet" "a_bug()"
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Open an issue with a minimal reproduction. The "
          html tag="code"
            text "create-twinkleplop-repro"
          text " CLI"
          soft_break
          text "			scaffolds one for you with the relevant package versions pinned."
        line_break
        line_break
        line_break
        paragraph
          text "Security issues should go to "
          html tag="a" href="mailto:security@twinkleplop.dev"
            text "security@twinkleplop.dev"
          soft_break
          text "			instead of the public tracker."
        line_break
        line_break
    line_break
    line_break
    html tag="FaqList" initial_open="01-0" sections=[object Object] self_closing=true
    line_break
    line_break
  line_break
  line_break
